WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.940
Adrenaline reaches a liver
cell and binds to its surface.

2
00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:09.030
Inside, the cell starts breaking down
its store of glycogen into glucose.

3
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.600
Only a few hormone molecules arrive.

4
00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:15.600
Yet thousands of glucose
molecules pour out of the cell.

5
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:20.370
How can so few hormone molecules
make a cell release so much sugar?

6
00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:24.160
In this mission, you'll find out
where a hormone's receptor sits,

7
00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.860
and why it sits there.

8
00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:30.300
Then you'll see how a hormone's signal
gets past the membrane and changes what

9
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:31.700
the cell does.

10
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:36.920
Your mission: explain how a few hormone
molecules can make a cell release thousands

11
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:38.190
of sugar molecules.
